          "text": "## Primary solution\n\nThe pattern indexes as **body-centered tetragonal**, with \\(a=4.1439\\) \u00c5 and \\(c=10.2259\\) \u00c5. The relative intensities, particularly of 101/103-type reflections, favor **ordered Ir/Ru occupation** of the parent ThCr\\(_2\\)Si\\(_2\\) transition-metal site. The resulting space group is noncentrosymmetric **\\(I\\bar{4}m2\\) (No. 119)**. Ir/Ru site interchange represents the indistinguishable inverse-domain model.\n\n```cif\ndata_CeIrRuGe2_ordered\n_audit_creation_method                 'Indexed and modeled from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common                  'cerium iridium ruthenium digermanide'\n_chemical_formula_structural           'CeIrRuGe2'\n_chemical_formula_sum                  'Ce1 Ge2 Ir1 Ru1'\n_chemical_formula_weight               578.66\n\n_cell_length_a                         4.1439(2)\n_cell_length_b                         4.1439(2)\n_cell_length_c                         10.2259(8)\n_cell_angle_alpha                      90\n_cell_angle_beta                       90\n_cell_angle_gamma                      90\n_cell_volume                           175.60(3)\n_cell_formula_units_Z                  2\n\n_space_group_crystal_system            tetragonal\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt              'I -4 m 2'\n_space_group_IT_number                 119\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type                 'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength           1.5406\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn          10.95\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\n_atom_site_adp_type\nCe1  Ce  2  a  0.00000  0.00000  0.00000   1.000  0.0050  Uiso\nIr1  Ir  2  c  0.00000  0.50000  0.25000   1.000  0.0050  Uiso\nRu1  Ru  2  d  0.00000  0.50000  0.75000   1.000  0.0050  Uiso\nGe1  Ge  4  e  0.00000  0.00000  0.367(2)  1.000  0.0050  Uiso\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing is:\n\n| \\(2\\theta_{\\rm obs}\\) | Reflection |\n|---:|:---|\n| 17.33\u00b0 | 002 |\n| 23.14\u00b0 | 101 |\n| 34.03\u00b0 | 103 |\n| 35.08\u00b0 | 004 |\n| 35.28\u00b0 | 112 |\n| 43.65\u00b0 | 200 |\n| 47.14\u00b0 | 114 |\n| 47.30\u00b0 | 202 |\n| 63.44\u00b0 | 220 |\n\nA disordered centrosymmetric \\(I4/mmm\\) model with Ir/Ru sharing 4d gives the same peak positions, but is disfavored by the observed intensities of odd-\\(l\\) reflections such as 101 and 103. Swapping Ir and Ru between 2c and 2d is an inverse-domain choice and cannot be distinguished from this powder pattern.",
